<Layout title="About — Zahin Kabir" active="About"><section class="wrap page-top"><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT / ZAHIN KABIR</p><h1>Hi, I’m Zahin.</h1><p class="lede">I study Chemical Engineering at Purdue and spend a lot of my time working on hardware.</p></section><section class="wrap prose-grid"><h2>What I’ve been doing</h2><div><p>I’m expecting to graduate in 2027. So far, I’ve worked on research equipment at Shinkei Systems, coffee-processing and test-equipment projects at Keurig Dr Pepper, and indigo extraction at Ourobio. At the moment, I’m also building a small coffee roaster.</p><p>I like work where I can move between a CAD model, the actual hardware, and the data coming out of it. Sometimes that means making a bracket or welding a frame; sometimes it means debugging a script or figuring out why an experiment didn’t work.</p><p>I’m interested in mechanical engineering, robotics, hardware, R&D, mechatronics, automation, and product-development roles.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${base}experience/`}>See where I’ve worked ↗</a></div></section></Layout>
